  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1502.15 “Dredge” as a verb means to make a body of water such as a lake, river, channel, harbor, or other area of surface water or wetland wider, deeper, or cleaner by",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1502.15 “Dredge” as a verb means to make a body of water such as a lake, river, channel, harbor, or other area of surface water or wetland wider, deeper, or cleaner by the removal of sand, silt, mud, rock, or other such material.\n\nSource. #9343, eff 1-1-09; ss by #12342, eff 8-15-17 (formerly Env-Wq 1502.14); ss by #14472, eff 1-19-26, EXPIRES: 1-19-36 (formerly Env-Wq 1502.17)",
